design:
Use a singleton table: `campaign_rules_binding(id, base_system_id, base_pack_id, base_version, addons_json, resolved_at)`. Keep add-ons JSON typed through `jsonColumn`. Existing code paths that create a campaign should write the default binding unless a caller passes another resolved binding.

Initial test sketch:
```ts
const info = createCampaign(db, { campaignId: 'c1', pack: EMBERFALL_HOLLOW });
expect(info.rulesBinding.base.systemId).toBe('dnd5e-srd');
expect(readCampaignRulesBinding(db)?.base.packId).toBe('dnd5e-srd-core');
```
